   "body": "When using AF_PACKET mode without hugepage enabled (PlainPacketPool is created), the PFrag initialization fails at this ip_frag.cc line:\r\n`indirect_pktmbuf_pool = new bess::DpdkPacketPool();`\r\n\r\nThe upf.json configuration used is below.\r\n  ip_frag_with_eth_mtu: 1518\r\n  max_ip_defrag_flows: 1000\r\n\r\nWithout frag/defrag enabled, we see outgoing GTP encapsulated packets being dropped after the Bess output queue in some scenarios where the total packet length exceeds the access interface MTU size.\r\n\r\nIt is not clear if this is an invalid configuration, i.e., frag/defrag indeed depends on DPDK mode, or a bug.\r\n\r\nAlso, please consider enabling the frag/defrag modules by default. \r\n\r\nLogs attached. Additional details can be found at the slack sdcore-dev thread below:\r\n[https://app.slack.com/client/T095Z193Q/C02TGUWTC93/thread/C02TGUWTC93-1661199350.360879](url)\r\n[upf.log](https://github.com/omec-project/upf/files/11215348/upf.log)\r\n",
